<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>Deutsche Welle: DW.com</title><subtitle type="html">Deutsche Welle: DW.com</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia</id><updated>2026-09-02T19:28:39Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-asia" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/s-12758?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-asia" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>US sanctions halt TOEFL and GRE tests in Iran, disrupting study plans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f682212c5d572f56c794488afb00b0084cf541c9719ad206715eb2230bc13c0f</id><updated>2026-09-02T19:28:36Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T14:56:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/us-sanctions-halt-toefl-and-gre-tests-in-iran-disrupting-study-plans/a-78764639--69744696120d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/us-sanctions-halt-toefl-and-gre-tests-in-iran-disrupting-study-plans/a-78764639?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Students in Iran can no longer take TOEFL and GRE exams after a US sanctions exemption was suspended. Applicants say the move threatens university deadlines and adds costly travel obligations.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>India rejects Hague ruling on Indus waters: What's next?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3cb9e8cfe4ea53e86e197738fcdccbc10d6497edbf9ced597a16511c9efee90d</id><updated>2026-09-02T19:28:39Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T13:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-rejects-hague-ruling-on-indus-waters-what-s-next/a-78753249--f1f03d136f38.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-rejects-hague-ruling-on-indus-waters-what-s-next/a-78753249?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">By rejecting an international arbitration panel's ruling, New Delhi has cast fresh doubt on the future of the 1960 Indus Waters Treaty.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Hong Kong activist Joshua Wong pleads guilty to collusion</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bf907fec3ab11838a15317949baaf53730949e6a8056d73c936f0ce799a2e2b1</id><updated>2026-09-02T19:26:29Z</updated><published>2026-09-02T02:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/hong-kong-activist-joshua-wong-pleads-guilty-to-collusion/a-78657525--a2b1f680bbe5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/hong-kong-activist-joshua-wong-pleads-guilty-to-collusion/a-78657525?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The prominent activist pleaded guilty to colluding with foreign entities. He faces a lengthy prison sentence.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>As glaciers melt, can communities be protected?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e5b4eb5d11de0c9ea69658784220eee1dcbd4526cfe9c2f4321b1723baee411f</id><updated>2026-09-02T19:26:29Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T13:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-glaciers-melt-can-communities-be-protected/a-78615775--1f4c55c04fcb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-glaciers-melt-can-communities-be-protected/a-78615775?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rising temperatures are increasing the risk of floods and avalanches in mountain regions. The disaster in Nepal and Tibet shows the urgent need for solutions, and the tools that could help save lives.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>Will Bangladesh join the Mecca defense alliance?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e49f12e46a915dece598cacf3f2aec59d928ae8643046f2f7a7e8c78a82dcc0</id><updated>2026-09-02T19:26:29Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T12:40:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/will-bangladesh-join-the-mecca-defense-alliance/a-78613944--650fbd31b54b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/will-bangladesh-join-the-mecca-defense-alliance/a-78613944?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">While Bangladesh weighs the risks of signing the Mecca Joint Defense Agreement, experts warn that such a move could complicate relations with neighboring India.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Nepal flood: Death toll tops 1,000 as rescue continues</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0c8ea97d3a430e11fa29c31d8171bc3eb5308fe6fe4f9149a7569cbe3c760361</id><updated>2026-09-02T19:26:29Z</updated><published>2026-09-01T10:53:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/nepal-flood-death-toll-tops-1-000-as-rescue-continues/a-78589460--34fefae74285.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/nepal-flood-death-toll-tops-1-000-as-rescue-continues/a-78589460?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Nepalese authorities say 4,000 people remain unaccounted for as rescue teams with search dogs comb through mud, rocks and debris.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>How China buried Tibet flood images after Nepal disaster</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:782140b2ef719d6a7f3b8a3661ea7a320d177ac1fdc821884dc68ba85a42ad85</id><updated>2026-09-02T19:26:29Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T14:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/how-china-buried-tibet-flood-images-after-nepal-disaster/a-78576472--7e7c26844487.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/how-china-buried-tibet-flood-images-after-nepal-disaster/a-78576472?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In Tibet, a digital crackdown followed the deadly flood that has devastated communities along the China-Nepal border. Censors erased viral footage while Chinese state media flooded platforms with official content.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>With multilateralism in decline, what's next for the world?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a81d8ffc03856ab4acaad6763dddaa704ba9629e65fec8283543140779df579f</id><updated>2026-09-02T19:26:29Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T11:13:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/with-multilateralism-in-decline-what-s-next-for-the-world/a-78555977--8df5725f7fb9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/with-multilateralism-in-decline-what-s-next-for-the-world/a-78555977?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The global political architecture is shifting, partly as a result of the actions of US President Donald Trump. As nations search for a new world order, some may gain influence and power, while others have much to lose.</summary><category term="TOP STORIES" /></entry><entry><title>Inside the sea cucumber smuggling boom</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f3d3c09316d40f86da8db05f229a41e1888fdd1e826a3427168f63e03f1bcaa7</id><updated>2026-09-02T19:26:29Z</updated><published>2026-08-31T10:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/inside-the-sea-cucumber-smuggling-boom/a-78005662--0b2701be2732.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/inside-the-sea-cucumber-smuggling-boom/a-78005662?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A quiet multimillion‑dollar black market is exploding across the Indian Ocean, driven by one unlikely animal: the sea cucumber.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>India's citizen-led school audits test limits of activism</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:bdd8f191e47608801375af4f52dce310c05fe5cc065ffcb9508a72c8b4ebe6a2</id><updated>2026-09-02T19:26:29Z</updated><published>2026-08-30T09:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/india-s-citizen-led-school-audits-test-limits-of-activism/a-78545789--a961d5089d76.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/india-s-citizen-led-school-audits-test-limits-of-activism/a-78545789?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The student-led "Cockroach" movement is taking its campaign for accountability to government schools, but the activists' methods are encountering growing resistance from authorities.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>South Korea leans toward military conscription for women</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:812167d24af450dd8684a7631a69f8fe2f3d28d086ce24ab62a1e92af8078e04</id><updated>2026-09-02T19:26:29Z</updated><published>2026-08-29T07:21:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/south-korea-leans-toward-military-conscription-for-women/a-78547426--a0344d8b90da.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/south-korea-leans-toward-military-conscription-for-women/a-78547426?maca=en-rss-en-asia-5133-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Facing a population decline, fewer potential service members and calls for social equality to be extended to national military service, Korea is inching closer to breaking the taboo on women on the front line.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
